  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S026",
      "patient_response": "Hi Dr. Smith. Nice to meet you too, I guess. Well, what brings me in is... I mean, things have just gotten really off lately, specifically with my eating. It's just completely out of whack. Usually, I'm a pretty steady eater, you know? Working in healthcare support, you really need your energy. You're on your feet all day, helping patients, moving around the unit, so you have to fuel up. \n\nBut lately... I don't know, some days I wake up and I barely manage to get down a cup of black coffee and maybe a granola bar before a whole shift. I just stare at food and can't bring myself to eat an actual meal. And it's really starting to show, which is part of why I decided I needed to come in. I put my scrubs on the other morning—the exact same ones I've been wearing for over a year—and they were just hanging loose off me. The waistband was falling down, the top was all baggy around my shoulders... and the thing is, I’m not even trying to lose weight at all. I haven't been on a diet or anything, it's just happening because my appetite is completely gone, and I just can't seem to get it back on track no matter how much I know I need the calories for work. It's just falling off me.",
