    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt this way before in your life, perhaps a few years ago or at another time, or is this the first time you have ever experienced these symptoms?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, no, it's not the first time I've ever felt down in my life, obviously, but this specific... this relentless kind of heaviness? It hasn't been a lifelong thing, if that's what you're asking. But it's also not just a recent thing, either. It's actually been going on for a really long time now. \n\nIt all started... gosh, it has to be almost two years ago now. Yeah, two years. That's when the clinic decided to do this massive overhaul of our Electronic Medical Records system—the EMR—and they completely restructured our entire workflow along with it. It was supposed to make everything more \"efficient,\" you know? But what it actually meant was that they completely changed my hours. I went from having this really predictable, steady schedule that I had built my whole life around, to suddenly having these erratic shifts, sometimes early mornings, sometimes late evenings, and it just threw my entire routine into chaos. \n\nAnd I remember, at first, I just thought I was tired from the adjustment. You know, learning the new software, trying to figure out the new charting requirements, dealing with the frustrated providers who couldn't figure out how to put in their orders... it was stressful for everyone. But then the stress didn't go away. The new system settled in, everyone else seemed to adapt, but I just... didn't. That's when this hollow feeling really started creeping in. I can almost trace it back to those first few weeks of the new schedule, trying to force myself to care about the new protocols, and just feeling this absolute wall of exhaustion and emptiness hit me. And it just never lifted. It's been almost two years of dragging myself through these shifts, two years of waking up and feeling like I have nothing left to give, two years of my workbench sitting there collecting dust. So, no, it's not brand new, but it's been this one long, continuous slide ever since that whole workflow overhaul upended everything.",
